## 4. Python Environment Setup

### Creating a project and virtual environment

I created a project folder named `python_setup_lab` on my Desktop and created a Python virtual environment.

```powershell
mkdir python_setup_lab
cd python_setup_lab
python -m venv venv
```

I activated the virtual environment in PowerShell:

```powershell
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass
.\venv\Scripts\Activate.ps1
```

The terminal displayed `(venv)`, confirming that the virtual environment was active.

### Installing and verifying a package

I installed the `requests` library and verified the installed packages.

```powershell
python -m pip install requests
python -m pip list
```

The installation completed successfully. The environment included `requests` and its dependencies: `certifi`, `charset-normalizer`, `idna`, and `urllib3`.

I exported the package versions to a requirements file:

```powershell
python -m pip freeze > requirements.txt
Get-Content requirements.txt
```

The `requirements.txt` file records the installed package versions so that the environment can be recreated later using:

```powershell
python -m pip install -r requirements.txt
```

